 dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is not dashed.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"placement","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation."}]}]},{"name":"orientation","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The orientation attribute indicates whether slurs and ties are overhand (tips down) or underhand (tips up). This is distinct from the placement attribute used by any notation type.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"bezierX","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point for one with a stop or continue type.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"bezierY","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point for one with a stop or continue type.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"bezierX2","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a continue type.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"bezierY2","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a continue type.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"bezierOffset","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point offset for one with a stop or continue type. Deprecated as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bezierX"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"bezierOffset2","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur with a continue type. Deprecated as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bezierX2"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlur"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"title":"MXLTenths","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the middle of a staff line."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSlur/init(i